@packages/sigilc/sources.sigil from SigilSourceIdentity import { CompilerInputSelection }

component SigilComparisonScope {
  goal {
    Resolve requested roots into reproducible *DesignMembership* and
    implementation selection for library callers.
  }

  constraints {
    *StructuralScope* Accept version 1 scope input with workspace-relative design
    roots and an implementation selection. Reject unknown fields, duplicate or
    missing roots, paths outside the workspace, and empty selections unless
    explicitly allowed. compiler.sigil is an ordinary source; imports do not
    imply runtime calls or semantic dependence.
  }

  cases {
    *DependencyClosure* Selecting a source that imports another includes the
    provider and records why it was included. Cycles include each source once.
    An unresolved import adds no target and remains a diagnostic on its source.

    *ScopeChanges* Reordering roots changes focus order while preserving
    membership identity. Removing a source from membership does not delete it or
    its stored reading.
  }

  interface {
    *ScopeInput* Resolve a versioned scope object containing ordered design roots
    and a CompilerInputSelection for implementation sources. Report malformed
    input as an error and expose resolution as a library operation, without
    adding a scope command.

    *FocusOrder* Preserve requested root order as focus priority. List dependency
    additions deterministically after roots with their inclusion reasons. Report
    order separately from unordered membership; order does not schedule
    interpreters.

    DesignMembership Close roots over resolved import targets, owners of
    imported names, and owners of entities or Facets in each included source.
    Include each owner source and record its reason. Preserve physical source
    and canonical owner for every unit, plus applicable configuration, glossary
    context, global diagnostics, and unresolved references. Report roots and
    dependency additions separately; do not infer membership from prose or
    caller metadata.
  }
}
